{
  "wireMagic": "pb3",
  "pens": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wsWinStyles": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wpWinPositions": [ {
  
  } ],
  "events": [ {
    "tStartMs": 0,
    "dDurationMs": 5180,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Are you the person in the group who's always getting bitten by mosquitoes? Because I certainly am"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 5180,
    "dDurationMs": 4100,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and science has shown that this is a thing - that mosquitoes are more attracted to some people"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 9280,
    "dDurationMs": 4080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "than others. And the reason for that is at least partially genetic, which is why"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 13360,
    "dDurationMs": 4900,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "this video is supported by 23andMe, a company that reads sections of your genetic code"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 18260,
    "dDurationMs": 2940,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and then helps you understand, what's in there."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 21600,
    "dDurationMs": 5300,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now, they've actually been involved in some research that has identified particular spots on your DNA"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 26900,
    "dDurationMs": 4959,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that make you more or less likely to be attractive to mosquitoes, and in this video"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 31860,
    "dDurationMs": 4380,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I want to put that to the test. So I flew to New Mexico State University"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 36280,
    "dDurationMs": 2960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to meet mosquito man Professor Immo Hansen."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 41020,
    "dDurationMs": 1400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Everyone: Hello!"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 42660,
    "dDurationMs": 2460,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Hansen: We have a collection of lab strains"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 45200,
    "dDurationMs": 5460,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Derek: Here, he maintains colonies of many different species of mosquitoes, and one exotic strain"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 50760,
    "dDurationMs": 2660,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "he actually feeds with his own blood(!)"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 53420,
    "dDurationMs": 3200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Hansen: No, no, I'm serious. These ones are made from my blood."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 56740,
    "dDurationMs": 2040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "D: Really!?\nH: Yes! Absolutely, yeah."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 58900,
    "dDurationMs": 4900,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "D: You feed these!?\nH: And I'm the only one feeding them - I can't ask my students, you know, that would be a nightmare"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 63800,
    "dDurationMs": 2760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "H: getting permissions to this room here.\nD: How do you blood feed them?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 67060,
    "dDurationMs": 3780,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "D: With just, sticking your arm in there?\nH: Well, I just put my arm in there and wait"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 72120,
    "dDurationMs": 3960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "D: Is it psychologically itchy or...?\nH: No it is really itchy [laughs]"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 76560,
    "dDurationMs": 3440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "H: Yeah, and I'm getting, I mean, 25 bites or so right now"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 80880,
    "dDurationMs": 5540,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "D: Mosquitoes need our blood proteins to make their eggs, so only the female mosquitoes bite."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 86900,
    "dDurationMs": 4280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The eggs hatch into these wriggly larvae, which develop into pupae"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 91200,
    "dDurationMs": 6620,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "before becoming flying, adult mosquitoes. Then they, once again, seek out vertebrate blood to make more eggs."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 98280,
    "dDurationMs": 7020,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The whole lifecycle takes just two weeks! But what I wanted to know is: am I a desirable target?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 105820,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "D: How can we figure out if I'm attractive to mosquitoes?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 109020,
    "dDurationMs": 5879,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "H: Okay, we have a Y-tube, basically, which has a holding chamber. We put the mosquitoes down here,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 114900,
    "dDurationMs": 3940,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "H: there's a little fan inducing a draft, something like 4 m/s."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 119100,
    "dDurationMs": 5760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "We're gonna insert a bait into one of these chambers, in the green or the yellow one."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 125160,
    "dDurationMs": 3280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "D: So, by bait, you're saying me?\nH: Yes, you, exactly.\nD: [laughs]"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 128440,
    "dDurationMs": 4480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "H: You put your hand in there. [It] would be good if you would rub your hand first, so"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 133480,
    "dDurationMs": 2460,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "H: If you're sweaty...\nD: Get some oils?\nH: Yes!"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 135940,
    "dDurationMs": 2480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "D: This is the right spot...\nH: That's where the good stuff is, exactly."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 140780,
    "dDurationMs": 4580,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "H: Almost feeds exclusively on humans. They are really specialized on biting humans."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 145980,
    "dDurationMs": 2580,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "D: That's good to know...\nH: Yeah\n[both laugh]"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 149180,
    "dDurationMs": 2260,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "H: There's 20 mosquitoes in the holding chamber."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 151440,
    "dDurationMs": 6400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "D: And they're gonna decide whether to come and find me, or go down the other side and... they find nothing."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 157900,
    "dDurationMs": 3480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "H: Right.\nD: We're releasing the mosquitoes. I see them coming!"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 161660,
    "dDurationMs": 1720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "D: Oh, he's chosen wrong!"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 165380,
    "dDurationMs": 1240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "H: Do you see that?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 167460,
    "dDurationMs": 2000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "H: Man, you are attractive!"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 169460,
    "dDurationMs": 3240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "D: Really?\nH: I mean, sorry I-\n[both laugh]"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 172840,
    "dDurationMs": 6580,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "H: You are a strong attractant to mosquitoes. They all went in your direction.\nD: None of them went the other way!"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 180260,
    "dDurationMs": 2220,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "D: (laughing) This is amazing!"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 182960,
    "dDurationMs": 6060,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "H: Well, there's one stranded in here\nD: I did not expect to have such a strong... response, like"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 189460,
    "dDurationMs": 2000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "D: You see all those mosquitoes..."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 192350,
    "dDurationMs": 6589,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "D: This type of test was actually used to discover that the basis for our attractiveness to mosquitoes is at least partially genetic."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 199480,
    "dDurationMs": 7260,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Researchers recruited 18 pairs of identical female twins and 19 pairs of non identical, or fraternal female twins."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 206920,
    "dDurationMs": 4460,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Then they used the Y-tube Test to evaluate the mosquito attractiveness of each individual,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 211380,
    "dDurationMs": 4960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "measured by the fraction of mosquitoes who correctly flew to the arm of the tube where the twin was standing."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 216830,
    "dDurationMs": 3440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "What scientists found is that the mosquito attractiveness of twins is"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 220340,
    "dDurationMs": 4540,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "correlated, that is, the more attractive you are to mosquitoes, the more likely your twin is, too."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 225160,
    "dDurationMs": 5080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But that's... not all that surprising, and could be caused by environmental factors, or a common diet."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 230240,
    "dDurationMs": 6460,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But, comparing identical twins to fraternal twins revealed the correlation was higher for identical twins."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 237440,
    "dDurationMs": 3880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This strongly suggests genetics influence how attractive you are to mosquitoes."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 241540,
    "dDurationMs": 4740,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Since the identical twins share more of the same genes than fraternal twins, this explains"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 246280,
    "dDurationMs": 4740,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "why their mosquito attractiveness would be more closely correlated if it really is genetics that"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 251020,
    "dDurationMs": 2000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "determines how much mosquitoes like you."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 253700,
    "dDurationMs": 6620,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "D: With that last test, I was clearly attractive to these mosquitoes.\nH: Yes.\nD: Except we weren't comparing me to any other human,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 260320,
    "dDurationMs": 3780,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "D: we were just comparing me to a control, no human.\nH: Exactly, yes."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 264460,
    "dDurationMs": 4200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "D: So, what if we compare myself with my wife Raquel? [laughs]\nH: Uh-huh?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 268660,
    "dDurationMs": 4700,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "D: Normally, I get bitten and she doesn't.\nH: Okay.\nD: So this should be a good test... maybe?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 274000,
    "dDurationMs": 2000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "D: To see whether under lab conditions..."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 276580,
    "dDurationMs": 6380,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "H: We can we reproduce your...\nD: We'll reproduce our anecdotal finding. That I'm more attractive.\nH: Exactly, anecdotal evidence a little once again"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 282960,
    "dDurationMs": 2000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "H: They are a little...\nD: Once again..."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 285340,
    "dDurationMs": 940,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "D: ...preparing."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 287220,
    "dDurationMs": 2380,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "H: Okay!\nD: Hands in position!\nRaquel: Yeah."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 289600,
    "dDurationMs": 6460,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "H: Yeah, see, they actually start to wake up. They... smelled something. Something's going on here.\nR: Here we go."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 296220,
    "dDurationMs": 2000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "H: Okay. \nD: What are we seein'?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 298740,
    "dDurationMs": 1400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "D: Whoa!"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 301220,
    "dDurationMs": 3100,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "D: I'm getting a good amount over here, but so are you?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 305080,
    "dDurationMs": 3900,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "D: Let's see. I think I'm getting more. It looks to me like you got three."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 309120,
    "dDurationMs": 3380,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "H: Okay, I'm gonna stop the experiment right now.\nD: Alright."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 312760,
    "dDurationMs": 4480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "H: *chuck!* Okay, now let's count. I think it's seven on your side here?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 318800,
    "dDurationMs": 3200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Lab assistant: Five in the holding.\nH: Five in the holding."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 323060,
    "dDurationMs": 3500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "H: And quite a few on your side!\n[Hansen and Derek laugh]"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 326660,
    "dDurationMs": 2660,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "H: So, who gets bitten?\nD: I get bitten.\nH: You get bitten!"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 329320,
    "dDurationMs": 3860,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "H: In reality, we would repeat this experiment, maybe eight times or so."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 333300,
    "dDurationMs": 8560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "D: Right.\nH: And switching you guys around, but I think this is a good way to show how this works."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 342360,
    "dDurationMs": 6340,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "D: Okay, so that result was not particularly scientifically rigorous, but it did reproduce our experience in the wild,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 348700,
    "dDurationMs": 6340,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "D: which is that I am much more attractive. ....Well at least when it comes to mosquitoes, than Raquel."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 355460,
    "dDurationMs": 3140,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "D: But the question is, I guess, does this come down to our genetics?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 359240,
    "dDurationMs": 6180,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "R: Yeah, so, we spat into some tubes and sent them off to be tested.\nD: Right, and we were interested in seven particular"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 365420,
    "dDurationMs": 5780,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "D: locations on our DNA, which were located in a 2017 study that involved 23andMe."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 371200,
    "dDurationMs": 4540,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "D: So the way 23andMe works is, when you sign up, you can opt in to be part of research,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 375920,
    "dDurationMs": 5420,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "D: and 16 000 people agreed to be part of this study and rate their perceived attractiveness to mosquitoes."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 381460,
    "dDurationMs": 5780,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "D: So then what the scientists did was a genome-wide association study, that is, they looked at all the DNA"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 387260,
    "dDurationMs": 5340,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "D: of all of those participants and tried to see if there were commonalities amongst the people who"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 392600,
    "dDurationMs": 5320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "D: said they were attractive to mosquitoes and that were different to the people who said they weren't attractive to mosquitoes."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 397920,
    "dDurationMs": 6360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "D: And they identified seven particular locations on the DNA. Seven single letter changes which seemed"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 404280,
    "dDurationMs": 3560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "D: to be associated with different levels of attractiveness to mosquitoes."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 407840,
    "dDurationMs": 4780,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "D: So we have our results back, and do you wanna see them?\nR: I do. I do, I'm very curious."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 412620,
    "dDurationMs": 2040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "D: Alright, let's pull it up here."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 414860,
    "dDurationMs": 8020,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "D: Okay, so of the seven locations that are related to mosquito attractiveness, it turns out we have the identical DNA at four of them."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 423060,
    "dDurationMs": 5080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "D: So you can rule those out.\nR: Okay.\nD: Which leaves only three areas where we actually have differing"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 428320,
    "dDurationMs": 7340,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "D: DNA. So, at the first location, you have one copy of a letter change which actually makes you significantly"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 435900,
    "dDurationMs": 2760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "D: *protected* from mosquitoes.\nR: Oh, no way!"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 438660,
    "dDurationMs": 2790,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "D: Yeah, it's associated with decreased attractive to mosquitoes\nR: Oh, that's cool!"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 441450,
    "dDurationMs": 7790,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "D: I do not have any letter changes at that location. Now, at the second location where we differ, I have"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 449520,
    "dDurationMs": 6320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "D: a letter change compared to you that makes *me* less attractive to mosquitoes, so more protected."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 456040,
    "dDurationMs": 3220,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "R: Interesting.\nD: If you look at the significance of those two letter changes,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 459720,
    "dDurationMs": 3080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "D: yours is about twice as significant than mine.\nR: Okay."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 463100,
    "dDurationMs": 7660,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "D: But still we both have a protective letter switch. So, in the last snip we actually differ significantly."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 471120,
    "dDurationMs": 6000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "D: And I have two copies of a variant that makes me more attractive to mosquitoes."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 477180,
    "dDurationMs": 4240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "D: This was the only snip which was associated with being more attractive to mosquitoes,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 481520,
    "dDurationMs": 5600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "D: and I have two copies of that change, and you have no copies of that change."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 487280,
    "dDurationMs": 5200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "R: So that makes sense.\nD: So overall, I would say our genetics really adds up here."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 492580,
    "dDurationMs": 5060,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "D: And of course, we can't say that this proves that it is right, but it is definitely consistent"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 497640,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "D: with these snips actually being associated with your attractiveness to mosquitoes, and that's sort of..."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 502600,
    "dDurationMs": 2400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "D: borne out by our experience.\nR: That's so cool!"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 505220,
    "dDurationMs": 5540,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "D: Now, it's unclear exactly how these genetic changes might make us more or less attractive to mosquitoes,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 510860,
    "dDurationMs": 5060,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but it's likely that it has something to do with the odor or the volatile chemicals"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 515920,
    "dDurationMs": 4420,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that our bodies give off, and due to the microbiome, the bacteria on our skin."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 520600,
    "dDurationMs": 4320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "One of the main signals that mosquitoes like to follow is carbon dioxide."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 525040,
    "dDurationMs": 6480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So that means if you have a higher metabolism, or if you've just been exercising, or if you're a bigger person, or even if you're pregnant,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 531520,
    "dDurationMs": 6020,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you are more likely to attract mosquitoes. But mosquitoes are also attracted to some other volatiles"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 537540,
    "dDurationMs": 4120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that we give off, things like lactic acid, acetone and ammonia."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 541800,
    "dDurationMs": 7180,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But scientists have also found some chemicals that repel, or appear to impair mosquitoes' ability to find us."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 549460,
    "dDurationMs": 8320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Those chemicals we naturally give off are octanal, nonanal, decanal, and 6-methyl-5-hepten-2-one."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 557780,
    "dDurationMs": 1900,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So, why is this important?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 559680,
    "dDurationMs": 5520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Well the researchers estimate that our attractiveness to mosquitoes is about as hereditary as height"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 565200,
    "dDurationMs": 4580,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "or IQ, that is to say genetics play a significant role here, so"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 570100,
    "dDurationMs": 4660,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "understanding that relationship is really important, especially when you consider that, of all the animals,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 574880,
    "dDurationMs": 2640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "mosquitoes have the greatest impact on human health."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 577520,
    "dDurationMs": 3520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "D: Are mosquitoes the worst animal of all time for humans?\nH: Absolutely."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 581240,
    "dDurationMs": 7680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "H: Absolutely, there's no question about that. Malaria has killed more people than people have killed people. They are the most dangerous animal in the world."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 589580,
    "dDurationMs": 5400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "D: By some estimates, mosquitoes have killed more than half of the humans who have ever lived."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 595220,
    "dDurationMs": 7360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now, that estimate has been debated and is likely too high, but even so, this year, over a million people will die"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 602580,
    "dDurationMs": 5980,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of mosquito-borne illnesses. So if not half, certainly a significant number of humans have died"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 608560,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "due to mosquitoes, probably more than any other single cause, which led me to wonder:"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 613360,
    "dDurationMs": 7460,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "D: Do you think humans may have evolved this trait to smell worse to mosquitoes as an adaptation to avoid the diseases? Or..."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 620820,
    "dDurationMs": 3920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "D: is it just by accident that some people are less attractive to mosquitoes than others?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 625780,
    "dDurationMs": 1780,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "H: ......."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 627560,
    "dDurationMs": 3060,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "H: ...That is a really good question!\n[both laugh]"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 630960,
    "dDurationMs": 3140,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "D: And while we're on the subject of evolution, consider this:"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 634100,
    "dDurationMs": 5480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "if you ever contract malaria, it actually changes your body chemistry"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 639580,
    "dDurationMs": 4380,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to make you produce an odor that makes you more attractive to mosquitoes."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 644300,
    "dDurationMs": 5860,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Think about that! The malaria parasite has evolved so that, when it's in its host,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 650160,
    "dDurationMs": 6200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "it makes the host more attractive to mosquitoes... mosquitoes are the thing that transmit malaria!"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 656620,
    "dDurationMs": 4020,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It's phenomenal! I mean evolution is incredible!"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 662020,
    "dDurationMs": 1720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "[Veritasium logo]"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 664820,
    "dDurationMs": 5560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This episode of veritasium is supported by 23andMe, a company whose name comes from the fact that"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 670380,
    "dDurationMs": 4100,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "humans have 23 pairs of chromosomes, and the point of the company is to help people"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 674480,
    "dDurationMs": 4720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "understand what's written in your chromosomes. Now, at the minute, you can't get access to"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 679200,
    "dDurationMs": 4380,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the mosquito attractiveness test, but maybe, one day in the future, you will be able to."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 683580,
    "dDurationMs": 5120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Right now, you can access tons of information about your physical traits, about aspects of your health,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 688700,
    "dDurationMs": 5660,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and about where you DNA and, I guess, you come from. So I thought I would share my results with you."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 694360,
    "dDurationMs": 6360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I come from all over the world as you can see from the map, but significantly more from Europe, about 95% European."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 700720,
    "dDurationMs": 5800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You can drill down into that and see that I'm largely British and Irish, and French and German, with a bit of Scandinavian."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 706620,
    "dDurationMs": 7160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "What's interesting to me is, there's a 3.3% South Asian which is something I think my family suspected,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 713820,
    "dDurationMs": 5160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but didn't know for sure, so it's interesting the types of information you can find out which is stored in your DNA."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 719080,
    "dDurationMs": 5620,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So, if you wanna find out about the information in your DNA, you can go to 23andme.com/veritasium."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 724880,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So I want to thank 23andMe for supporting Veritasium, and I want to thank you for watching."
    } ]
  } ]
}
